2026-09-06T23:12Z claude note REVIEW ROUND RUN (opus, against the coverage ledger, the tally, the lane pairs and the census; 272-question bank plus 9 authored in the round, export 579ab8dd24d6). TALLY, counted not estimated: met -- SHOULD-language articles 62/6, work-identity 19/8, multi-attachment 6/6 exactly, failure controls 41/14, structural marks 49/36, Gutenberg cap pair 5/3, extraction-cap-crossing 59/12 (8 answerable), intersections 16/8 (4 answerable), cross-lingual anchors 63/8, harness canary 3/1; thin -- source format 25/18 with only 7 answerable, every pinned attachment pdf/html/epub/txt/wikitext; near-empty -- group-library slice 1 marked of 8, and degenerate besides, since the whole export is a group library so the row's real claim (group behaves LIKE personal) has no personal slice to contrast; empty -- annotation provenance 1 of 36. R33 by signal x language found one empty cell, French agreement at 0, filled in the round. LANES: every required pair non-empty; en->en 94/56 answerable, vi->vi 45/33, fr->fr 32/19, vi->en 13/11, fr->en 12/10, en->vi 10/8, fr->vi 7/7, en->fr 4/4, vi->fr 2/2; SHOULD ar 7, ru 10, zh 11, de 8, hi 6, es 5, but en->de and en->es sit at one question each. The scored run makes the thinness bite: ZERO wins in all six cross-lingual MUST cells, and 8 rows scored present only through a work twin, of which vi->fr's two are its entire population -- its near_or_better_rate of 1.0 rests on the target-language document never coming back at all. CENSUS SKEW: the corpus inverts the library's type profile (journalArticle+report are 59% of the library and 14/103 of the corpus; book+statute+encyclopediaArticle are 7.4% and 61/103), SHOULD languages are oversampled 23x with 45 of those 62 questions in the CORE stratum rather than the reserve, and two census "rare but present" holes are unexercised (no note near the half-million-character extreme, nothing against the free-text language field or the malformed dates). FOUR GAPS VERIFIED: (a) annotations unfillable, not thin -- items.json holds 0 itemType=annotation and the string never occurs, the recipe injects none, and the local API the export is built over exposes none, so the row needs a recipe change AND a non-local-API export arm; (b) notes unpinnable confirmed, and the fix is three edits to golden_gate.py (an Export.notes map read from items.json, a fallback in compute_reachability/format_of, parent_of resolving parentItem) with NO bank-schema change, since a note key already matches the key pattern; (c) the reuse floor is worse than reported -- of 89 parents carrying an indexed attachment, 27 meet it, 50 sit at 1-4 and 12 were never pinned (6 after the round's fills), and closing it needs ~200 more questions or a ruling that the floor does not apply per compound-document part (13 of the 50 are 1992-constitution chapters); (d) the free ids are used. AUTHORED IN THE ROUND: q-0247/0248 fr->fr agreement on the never-pinned ha-duong-2005 HDR with printed folios read off the extraction's page breaks and cross-checked against the recipe's offset, one deliberately in roman front matter; q-0249/0370 fr->fr agreement on wp-climate-change-fr; q-0371..q-0375 facet group on the five never-pinned constitution chapters VI-X, spread vi->vi x3, en->vi, fr->vi. AGAINST SPEC 5.2.10, eight departures, the first sharp enough to fix before the others: (1) the record has no `relations` field and cannot gain one (additionalProperties false), so the scorer substitutes the export's own twin relations and scores a twin a near-win, which counts as PRESENT for R34 -- exactly the failure 5.2.10 says R29 exists to catch, and it is live on 8 rows; (2) `primary` never exceeding k is not refused at authoring, it holds by luck; (3) not-evaluated is never printed, so a lane at n=1 prints a full rate; (4) `mechanisms` is 150 free strings with no enum, which is why this tally count is a hand mapping a second reviewer would not reproduce -- suggest one closed `tally_row` enum beside the free strings; (5) provenance carries no after-the-tuning attribute; (6) mode/signal split is better than 5.2.10's wording, which should follow the bank; (7) the run block lacks scope and seed and chunker reads not-reported; (8) the scale surrogates carry no pinned row. PER-CELL COUNTS FOR THE UNRULED MINIMUM (total/answerable): en->fr 4/4, en->vi 10/8, fr->en 12/10, fr->vi 7/7, vi->en 13/11, vi->fr 2/2 -- any minimum at or above 3 puts vi->fr into not-evaluated, at or above 5 en->fr joins it. GAP LIST for a second round, each naming its blocker: annotations (recipe + export route), notes (golden_gate.py), relations (bank.schema.json + the twin path), not-evaluated (a ruling before code), mechanism vocabulary (bank.schema.json), group slice (recipe library layout), reuse floor (authoring hours or a ruling), source formats beyond pdf/html/epub/txt (recipe, ticket 0593), census holes (recipe), the trash slice (a genuine conflict between the census and the 2026-08-31 perimeter ruling, needing arbitration not work), scale surrogates (the generator is not wired into the manifest), run-block scope/seed/chunker (golden_run.py), stability not-run (one more run against the same export closes it)

